cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the saved predictions, please cite this repository and the accompanying report."
title: "Evaluating a Small Open-Weight Large Language Model for Structured Information Extraction from Chest X-Ray Reports: A Comparison of Direct and Structure-Based Pipelines"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Ntimana"
    given-names: "Risuna"
    affiliation: "University of the Witwatersrand, Johannesburg"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - chest X-ray
  - radiology report labelling
  - CheXpert
  - Llama-3.2
  - low-rank adaptation
  - structured output
abstract: >-
  Evaluation of meta-llama/Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct on extracting 14 CheXpert
  observations from OpenI chest X-ray reports, comparing a direct pipeline
  that returns one label per line with a structure-based pipeline that returns
  a six-section anatomical JSON object, under zero-shot, 5-shot, and LoRA
  fine-tuned conditions.
